# NestJS Backend

## Module structure

Each domain feature under `apps/api/src/modules/<feature>/`:

```
<feature>/
├── <feature>.module.ts
├── <feature>.controller.ts
├── <feature>.service.ts
├── dto/                  # request/response DTOs with validation decorators
├── entities/ or types/   # domain types (if not Prisma-generated)
└── <feature>.spec.ts     # unit tests for business logic
```

## Patterns

- **Controllers**: route definitions, DTO binding, call service, return response. No Prisma calls in controllers.
- **Services**: business logic, authorization checks, state transitions, orchestration.
- **Prisma**: inject `PrismaService`; keep queries in a dedicated repository class when a service grows large.
- **DTOs**: use `class-validator` + `class-transformer`; validate every request body and query param.
- **Guards**: JWT auth guard globally; add participation/ownership guards per route where needed.
- **Exception filters**: map domain errors to `{ statusCode, message, errorCode }` consistently.

## Rental state transitions

Implement as a dedicated service method per transition with explicit precondition checks. Use Prisma transactions when updating rental + handover + audit records together.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — explicit transition with guards
async approvePickupPhotos(rentalId: string, renterId: string) {
  const rental = await this.findRentalForRenter(rentalId, renterId);
  if (rental.status !== RentalStatus.PICKUP_APPROVAL_PENDING) {
    throw new InvalidTransitionError(...);
  }
  // transition atomically
}
```

## Images

Accept upload metadata or presigned-URL flow. Store object-storage keys/URLs in MongoDB — never binary blobs.

## Config

Use `@nestjs/config` with Joi/Zod validation schema. Fail fast on missing required env vars at bootstrap.
